WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.352 --> 00:00:01.423
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.423 --> 00:00:04.275
My name is Evan Carmichael
my one word is believe.

00:00:04.275 --> 00:00:06.511
I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve all

00:00:06.511 --> 00:00:08.144
the major problems of the world.

00:00:08.144 --> 00:00:11.526
And today's message is make no excuses.

00:00:11.526 --> 00:00:13.544
Over to you, Jon Taffer.

00:00:13.544 --> 00:00:15.622
(rooster crows)

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:18.289
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:21.085
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:00:21.085 --> 00:00:25.326
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:25.326 --> 00:00:26.749
- As a consultant for 30 years,

00:00:26.749 --> 00:00:29.090
I learned everything there
is to learn about success.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.355
What you do to be successful.

00:00:31.355 --> 00:00:33.476
Management, marketing, costs.

00:00:33.476 --> 00:00:35.819
Everything in my whole life
was, this is what you do

00:00:35.819 --> 00:00:38.143
to be successful, this is
what you do to be successful.

00:00:38.143 --> 00:00:42.305
Now after 92 bar rescues,
I know more about failure

00:00:42.305 --> 00:00:45.106
than any consultant I've ever met.

00:00:45.106 --> 00:00:46.582
You didn't even have to
sell a drink to make money

00:00:46.582 --> 00:00:47.798
last night did you?

00:00:47.798 --> 00:00:49.448
Come here shake your,

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:52.322
give away his booze, and
leave with your money.

00:00:52.322 --> 00:00:55.513
There's a walk to failure,
there's a talk to failure.

00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:56.598
You can see it.

00:00:56.598 --> 00:01:00.772
And I found, because I've been
exposed to so much failure.

00:01:00.772 --> 00:01:02.884
'Cause remember as a
consultant, most people either

00:01:02.884 --> 00:01:05.474
have money or some level of
success if they're calling you.

00:01:05.474 --> 00:01:06.842
The people I go to in Bar Rescue

00:01:06.842 --> 00:01:08.752
can't afford to buy me lunch.

00:01:08.752 --> 00:01:10.447
I mean they are broke!

00:01:10.447 --> 00:01:12.549
So, when I take a look at

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:15.567
the terrible situation that they're in

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.606
and the pressure that I'm
under to turn them around,

00:01:17.606 --> 00:01:20.861
the fact of the matter is
the only chance that I have

00:01:20.861 --> 00:01:24.817
of making them successful, is
by making them accountable.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.345
So, in all of these rescues,

00:01:27.345 --> 00:01:29.987
I've found a common
denominator of failure.

00:01:29.987 --> 00:01:34.076
And it's excuses. So you wake
in the morning you're failing.

00:01:34.076 --> 00:01:36.893
It's in the middle of the
recession eight years ago

00:01:36.893 --> 00:01:39.290
so you blame it on the recession.

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:41.836
But even in the middle of the
recession somebody was making

00:01:41.836 --> 00:01:43.710
money in your town right?

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.835
So that excuse is bull.

00:01:45.835 --> 00:01:47.901
How about the excuse,
I'll blame the president,

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:51.934
blame Greece, the Euro is
affecting my income in New York.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.874
You can blame everything
in the world, you can blame

00:01:53.874 --> 00:01:56.029
the weather, the president,
the mayor, the city,

00:01:56.029 --> 00:01:59.106
construction, traffic,
snow, terrible this, that.

00:01:59.106 --> 00:02:02.190
But the fact of the matter is
you're failing because of you.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.400
Because in the snow somebody
made money, in the cold

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.961
somebody made money.

00:02:05.961 --> 00:02:06.946
In the heat.

00:02:06.946 --> 00:02:09.307
So every excuse is bull.

00:02:09.307 --> 00:02:11.615
You're failing because of you.

00:02:11.615 --> 00:02:14.228
So if you wake up in the
morning and look in the mirror

00:02:14.228 --> 00:02:15.996
and blame it on the president,

00:02:15.996 --> 00:02:17.835
you've got no reason to change.

00:02:17.835 --> 00:02:20.016
But if you wake up in the
morning and look in the mirror

00:02:20.016 --> 00:02:23.419
and say "I am a failure"
you're not going to like it.

00:02:23.419 --> 00:02:25.152
And now you have to change.

00:02:25.152 --> 00:02:28.300
So I force them to own failure.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.870
I will not allow them to
push it off on anything

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.542
but themselves.

00:02:32.542 --> 00:02:35.009
And when you own your
failure, you won't like it

00:02:35.009 --> 00:02:37.438
and then you'll own your success.

00:02:37.438 --> 00:02:39.431
- Successful people don't make excuses.

00:02:39.431 --> 00:02:41.211
Successful people don't complain.

00:02:41.211 --> 00:02:43.709
If you look at whoever
you want to look up to,

00:02:43.709 --> 00:02:45.384
look at the most successful
people in the world

00:02:45.384 --> 00:02:48.354
in any industry, look at
the top and look at how much

00:02:48.354 --> 00:02:49.556
they complain.

00:02:49.556 --> 00:02:51.065
They don't complain.

00:02:51.065 --> 00:02:53.168
When you complain, when
you blame something else,

00:02:53.168 --> 00:02:56.830
when it's the governments
fault or interest rates fault

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:58.950
or the bad economy's fault,
or your partner who screwed

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.164
you over, or the customers who don't care.

00:03:01.164 --> 00:03:03.108
As long as you can blame
somebody else right?

00:03:03.108 --> 00:03:05.268
The education system, your
parents, your friends,

00:03:05.268 --> 00:03:07.265
your upbringing, there's
always somebody else to blame

00:03:07.265 --> 00:03:09.482
and when you blame somebody else,

00:03:09.482 --> 00:03:11.154
when you're in that mindset,

00:03:11.154 --> 00:03:12.798
then you never grow.

00:03:12.798 --> 00:03:15.034
You're making things easy on yourself.

00:03:15.034 --> 00:03:16.654
It allows you to coast.

00:03:16.654 --> 00:03:19.329
It allows you to play life
super safe because it's

00:03:19.329 --> 00:03:21.885
not your fault that you're
not more successful.

00:03:21.885 --> 00:03:24.057
Of course it's not your fault,
that would be difficult.

00:03:24.057 --> 00:03:25.227
That would be hard.

00:03:25.227 --> 00:03:27.106
It's somebody else's fault
so you could just stay where

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.888
you are because people
are holding you back from

00:03:29.888 --> 00:03:32.297
accomplishing the thing
you want to accomplish.

00:03:32.297 --> 00:03:36.357
Where successful people
take responsibility

00:03:36.357 --> 00:03:38.106
for where they are in life.

00:03:38.106 --> 00:03:40.898
And they say, I don't
care about the government,

00:03:40.898 --> 00:03:42.692
I don't care who's
president, I don't care about

00:03:42.692 --> 00:03:45.066
regulations that you have
or things that you're

00:03:45.066 --> 00:03:46.403
holding me back on.

00:03:46.403 --> 00:03:48.959
I will still go out and get mine.

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:51.115
And of course there are other factors.

00:03:51.115 --> 00:03:54.257
Of course the country
you come from matters.

00:03:54.257 --> 00:03:56.983
Of course education you
had and the connections you

00:03:56.983 --> 00:03:58.153
had growing up.

00:03:58.153 --> 00:03:59.390
Of course it matters.

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:00.390
But so what?

00:04:01.672 --> 00:04:04.343
You have to play the
hand that you were dealt.

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:06.122
You have these cards.

00:04:06.122 --> 00:04:10.310
You have to play those cards
and you can have success.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.670
One of the things I love looking at,

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:13.810
and this is why I do
all of these profiles,

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.548
the successful, famous entrepreneurs.

00:04:15.548 --> 00:04:19.399
There is always somebody who
has done way more than you

00:04:19.399 --> 00:04:23.234
have done with way fewer
resources than you already have.

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:26.000
So no matter what terrible
situation that you have,

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:26.963
and I'm empathetic.

00:04:26.963 --> 00:04:29.197
Maybe you come from a broken home.

00:04:29.197 --> 00:04:30.743
Maybe you have a really severe disability

00:04:30.743 --> 00:04:32.712
that's physically holding
you back from doing

00:04:32.712 --> 00:04:34.206
some of the things that you want to do.

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:36.652
Maybe there's a lot of pressure on you.

00:04:36.652 --> 00:04:38.235
Maybe you have some disease.

00:04:38.235 --> 00:04:41.082
Maybe you have zero money
in your bank account.

00:04:41.082 --> 00:04:46.017
These are real pressures
and I'm empathetic to that.

00:04:46.017 --> 00:04:47.148
But so what?

00:04:47.148 --> 00:04:49.985
The longer you believe that
those things are going to hold

00:04:49.985 --> 00:04:51.965
you where you are then they will.

00:04:51.965 --> 00:04:56.334
There are people who
have worse conditions,

00:04:56.334 --> 00:05:00.782
less money, are in worse
situations and they came out of it

00:05:00.782 --> 00:05:04.160
and accomplished amazing
things because they believed

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.501
that they could.

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.817
And that somebody that looks
like you has gone on and

00:05:07.817 --> 00:05:10.604
accomplished big things, then you can too.

00:05:10.604 --> 00:05:14.153
And it only happens when
you accept responsibility

00:05:14.153 --> 00:05:15.924
for where you are in life.

00:05:15.924 --> 00:05:17.957
So I could look at my
YouTube channel and say

00:05:17.957 --> 00:05:21.670
"The YouTube algorithm
changed, the YouTube algorithm

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.016
is all over the place now,
I can't figure it out.

00:05:24.016 --> 00:05:25.653
Stupid YouTube for
changing their algorithm

00:05:25.653 --> 00:05:27.408
and hurting my videos."

00:05:27.408 --> 00:05:30.412
I'm pumped whenever the
YouTube algorithm changes.

00:05:30.412 --> 00:05:33.393
I'm so excited because the
people who are ahead of me

00:05:33.393 --> 00:05:35.291
and the people who are
getting all of the videos

00:05:35.291 --> 00:05:36.343
and all the views?

00:05:36.343 --> 00:05:37.984
The people who are complaining?

00:05:37.984 --> 00:05:38.817
I love it.

00:05:38.817 --> 00:05:40.951
Change it more cause I'm
going to figure it out.

00:05:40.951 --> 00:05:42.978
I love the process of figuring it out.

00:05:42.978 --> 00:05:45.702
Whenever there's chaos, I see opportunity.

00:05:45.702 --> 00:05:47.771
And that's what entrepreneurs do.

00:05:47.771 --> 00:05:50.358
The most important thing that
you need as an entrepreneur

00:05:50.358 --> 00:05:54.232
is not resources, it's resourcefulness.

00:05:54.232 --> 00:05:55.963
So no matter what is thrown at you,

00:05:55.963 --> 00:05:57.881
and you're going to get
a lot thrown at you.

00:05:57.881 --> 00:05:59.239
In your life you have already had a lot

00:05:59.239 --> 00:06:01.818
of stuff thrown at you and guess what,

00:06:01.818 --> 00:06:03.612
as an entrepreneur, you're
just going to get punched

00:06:03.612 --> 00:06:04.841
in the face again.

00:06:04.841 --> 00:06:05.956
It's going to get worse.

00:06:05.956 --> 00:06:07.951
You're going to get more thrown at you.

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:11.252
It's going to be eating
more crap for years.

00:06:11.252 --> 00:06:13.844
This is the life you signed
up for and on the other side

00:06:13.844 --> 00:06:15.594
is amazingness.

00:06:15.594 --> 00:06:18.557
So when you accept
responsibility for where you are.

00:06:18.557 --> 00:06:20.699
When you realize that in every situation,

00:06:20.699 --> 00:06:23.629
no matter how much outside
your control you think it is

00:06:23.629 --> 00:06:26.074
there's always something
that you can do to make your

00:06:26.074 --> 00:06:27.920
situation better.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.290
When you accept that full
responsibility and stop

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:33.332
making excuses, that's
when life starts to change.

00:06:33.332 --> 00:06:35.300
That's when your business
starts to explode.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.095
And that's when you
start to see the impact

00:06:37.095 --> 00:06:39.055
and financial wealth that you
want to create for yourself

00:06:39.055 --> 00:06:40.915
start to happen.

00:06:40.915 --> 00:06:42.321
So the question today is, I'm curious,

00:06:42.321 --> 00:06:46.488
what has typically been the
biggest excuse that you've had?

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:49.800
The biggest complaint that
you've had that you've

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.201
told other people that
as of today is over.

00:06:53.201 --> 00:06:54.511
Leave it in the comments below.

00:06:54.511 --> 00:06:55.822
Super curious to find out.

00:06:55.822 --> 00:06:57.848
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Tina.

00:06:57.848 --> 00:06:59.375
Tina thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:02.920
Your One Word and making
that calligraphy art.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.570
And your one word is love.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.388
I really appreciate that
and I'm glad you're enjoying

00:07:06.388 --> 00:07:07.593
the book.

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.269
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:07:09.269 --> 00:07:10.569
I believe in you.

00:07:10.569 --> 00:07:13.035
I hope you continue to believe
in yourself and whatever

00:07:13.035 --> 00:07:14.343
your one word is.

00:07:14.343 --> 00:07:16.636
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:19.421
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:07:19.421 --> 00:07:22.107
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:24.814
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:07:24.814 --> 00:07:28.481
(typewriter clacking)

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:30.817
- I don't believe in excuses.

00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:32.400
Because the thing about
it, when you make an excuse

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.155
the thing that you have
to realize about life,

00:07:34.155 --> 00:07:36.285
somebody has it 10 times worse than you.

00:07:36.285 --> 00:07:38.739
And you're making an excuse
because you're soft man.

00:07:38.739 --> 00:07:41.822
(audience applauds)

00:07:44.203 --> 00:07:45.487
I've never cheated myself.

00:07:45.487 --> 00:07:47.465
Ever since I was seven
years old and everything

00:07:47.465 --> 00:07:49.990
that I did, I took pride
in what I did and I firmly

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.455
believe the harder you work,

00:07:51.455 --> 00:07:52.949
the harder it is to surrender.

00:07:52.949 --> 00:07:54.636
You see a lot of people don't understand,

00:07:54.636 --> 00:07:56.420
if you go through life
and you cheat yourself,

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:58.301
there is going to come a
time when inner certain

00:07:58.301 --> 00:08:00.861
meets diversity and if you're
not who you are supposed to be

00:08:00.861 --> 00:08:02.661
and adversity will always
introduce you into who

00:08:02.661 --> 00:08:04.109
you really are.

00:08:04.109 --> 00:08:05.743
And if you haven't been working that hard,

00:08:05.743 --> 00:08:06.939
if you haven't been sacrificing.

00:08:06.939 --> 00:08:08.612
If you haven't been emptying that bucket.

00:08:08.612 --> 00:08:09.938
If you haven't been born an only,

00:08:09.938 --> 00:08:12.604
then every aspect of your
life is going to crush you.

00:08:12.604 --> 00:08:14.520
Is going to make you give up.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:15.477
Is going to make you stop.

00:08:15.477 --> 00:08:16.926
Is going to make you make excuses.

00:08:16.926 --> 00:08:18.542
But if you work hard,

00:08:18.542 --> 00:08:20.513
if you've got a certain
person in you that when

00:08:20.513 --> 00:08:22.573
you hit adversity and you hit opposition,

00:08:22.573 --> 00:08:24.082
and you want to make excuses.

00:08:24.082 --> 00:08:25.656
And that person inside of
you is saying "Man you ain't

00:08:25.656 --> 00:08:27.108
"built like that.

00:08:27.108 --> 00:08:28.945
"You know you're better than that.

00:08:28.945 --> 00:08:31.643
"You know you're not like that man."

00:08:31.643 --> 00:08:32.893
You deal with it and you keep going

00:08:32.893 --> 00:08:34.893
and you embrace it man.

00:08:34.893 --> 00:08:36.261
That's what life's about.

00:08:36.261 --> 00:08:37.849
That is how people get stronger.

00:08:37.849 --> 00:08:40.271
People don't get stronger
by you making excuses.

00:08:40.271 --> 00:08:42.285
People get stronger by when
you go through adversity

00:08:42.285 --> 00:08:43.970
when you go through trial and tribulation

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:45.526
and you look at it and when
it hits you in the face

00:08:45.526 --> 00:08:47.153
you back up a little bit
and it hits you again,

00:08:47.153 --> 00:08:48.700
you back up a little
bit, and you step back up

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:52.944
and you say "If that's all
you got, you in trouble!"

00:08:52.944 --> 00:08:54.662
- I was in Johannesburg a little while ago

00:08:54.662 --> 00:08:57.406
and I went through the airport

00:08:57.406 --> 00:09:00.991
and I went into the
men's room, or washroom

00:09:00.991 --> 00:09:02.635
or bathroom, however you want to call it.

00:09:02.635 --> 00:09:05.383
And so I walked into the
men's room and the first thing

00:09:05.383 --> 00:09:07.860
I hear is "Welcome to my office."

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:12.811
And this was the janitor at
the Johannesburg men's room.

00:09:12.811 --> 00:09:13.711
- That's funny.

00:09:13.711 --> 00:09:16.925
- Who janitorized, or I'll make up a word,

00:09:16.925 --> 00:09:19.516
cleaned the men's, the toilets,

00:09:19.516 --> 00:09:21.766
like Mozart composed music.

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:24.028
- Mm-hmm.

00:09:24.028 --> 00:09:26.093
- Now that man has no money.

00:09:26.093 --> 00:09:28.519
That man probably has
very little education.

00:09:28.519 --> 00:09:31.322
That man is judged by the world as having

00:09:31.322 --> 00:09:32.682
an unimportant job.

00:09:32.682 --> 00:09:33.515
- Right.

00:09:33.515 --> 00:09:35.931
- And that man is a hero,
could be a hero to millions

00:09:35.931 --> 00:09:36.764
of people.

00:09:36.764 --> 00:09:39.762
Why, because he actually saw
himself as the ambassador

00:09:39.762 --> 00:09:41.114
to South Africa.

00:09:41.114 --> 00:09:43.531
And his passion was palpable.

00:09:45.346 --> 00:09:48.332
And his visceral commitment
to doing work at the highest

00:09:48.332 --> 00:09:51.992
level was like you don't
see even from the CEOs.

00:09:51.992 --> 00:09:52.825
- Right.

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:54.454
- And all I'm saying is,

00:09:54.454 --> 00:09:57.777
even the person with the broken heart,

00:09:57.777 --> 00:10:00.351
the person who's down on their knees.

00:10:00.351 --> 00:10:02.670
Whether they see it or
not, they have a choice

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:04.757
to rise above their circumstances.

00:10:04.757 --> 00:10:07.868
And leadership and humanity
is a testament to the people

00:10:07.868 --> 00:10:08.839
who have done it.

00:10:08.839 --> 00:10:11.055
I mean you look at Mandela,

00:10:11.055 --> 00:10:13.138
27 years in imprisonment.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.599
When his son died, he
wasn't allowed to attend the

00:10:16.599 --> 00:10:18.284
funeral of his own son.

00:10:18.284 --> 00:10:21.911
He said that was one of the
great pains of his life.

00:10:21.911 --> 00:10:23.355
And what did he do?

00:10:23.355 --> 00:10:27.475
The victim looks at
something like that, torture,

00:10:27.475 --> 00:10:29.180
and says "I am broken."

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:32.504
And they give up and they
close their heart, they close

00:10:32.504 --> 00:10:35.446
their mind, they close their
creativity and they blame

00:10:35.446 --> 00:10:37.961
the rest of their life
on what happened to them.

00:10:37.961 --> 00:10:38.794
- Mm-hm.

00:10:38.794 --> 00:10:40.716
- But Mandela, what he chose
to to do, was to use it as

00:10:40.716 --> 00:10:43.383
an opportunity because actually,

00:10:44.592 --> 00:10:46.804
the things that break
your heart, if you choose,

00:10:46.804 --> 00:10:48.511
can open your heart.

00:10:48.511 --> 00:10:51.261
Fear, the world says fear is bad.

00:10:52.182 --> 00:10:55.404
Fear is only an opportunity
for bravery training.

00:10:55.404 --> 00:10:59.130
And what he did was he used
those 27 years of torture

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:03.132
to open himself mentally,
physically, emotionally,

00:11:03.132 --> 00:11:05.687
and spiritually to the point
where when he was released

00:11:05.687 --> 00:11:07.914
and became the President of South Africa,

00:11:07.914 --> 00:11:10.865
he invited his jailers
to sit in the front row

00:11:10.865 --> 00:11:13.591
at his inauguration and he
was asked why and he said,

00:11:13.591 --> 00:11:17.129
"Because if I don't,
I'd still be in prison."

00:11:17.129 --> 00:11:19.320
And that's a long way
of saying but, you know,

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.342
we do make excuses
because we are very good

00:11:22.342 --> 00:11:23.708
at self-deception.

00:11:23.708 --> 00:11:26.286
Because if we actually had
to face the responsibility

00:11:26.286 --> 00:11:28.534
of playing with our bigness in the world,

00:11:28.534 --> 00:11:31.878
we'd have to let go of our
addiction to our excuses

00:11:31.878 --> 00:11:33.822
and leave what's safe.

00:11:33.822 --> 00:11:35.093
Am I making sense?

00:11:35.093 --> 00:11:36.758
- No totally, no you're
totally making sense.

00:11:36.758 --> 00:11:38.023
- You'd have to leave what's safe.

00:11:38.023 --> 00:11:39.625
I mean we are addicted to crisis sometime.

00:11:39.625 --> 00:11:40.869
It makes no sense.

00:11:40.869 --> 00:11:42.122
We are addicted to pain.

00:11:42.122 --> 00:11:43.029
- Mm-hmm.

00:11:43.029 --> 00:11:44.943
- And we have to actually
leave the pain to go out

00:11:44.943 --> 00:11:48.040
to the possibility of pleasure
and joy and greatness.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:50.000
And believe it or not, that frightens us.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:50.833
- Right.

00:11:50.833 --> 00:11:53.302
- So we make these excuses
and then we blame people.

00:11:53.302 --> 00:11:55.512
Oh Joe or Robin, I don't
like the way he looks.

00:11:55.512 --> 00:11:58.228
He speaks differently but subconsciously,

00:11:58.228 --> 00:12:00.572
as you're suggesting, those
are just our protective

00:12:00.572 --> 00:12:02.437
mechanisms to avoid owning

00:12:02.437 --> 00:12:05.404
the responsibility of our--

00:12:05.404 --> 00:12:06.339
(whooshing)

00:12:06.339 --> 00:12:09.361
- What do you feel
separates good athletes from

00:12:09.361 --> 00:12:10.861
the best athletes?

00:12:12.396 --> 00:12:16.578
- I think it comes back to what
I was saying earlier about,

00:12:16.578 --> 00:12:19.661
I mean I think a lot of it is mental.

00:12:21.656 --> 00:12:24.545
You know if you want to do
something, and you want it

00:12:24.545 --> 00:12:27.595
that bad, you'll make sacrifices.

00:12:27.595 --> 00:12:30.380
And you know growing up for me as a kid,

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:33.642
I made a lot of sacrifices
that I didn't see them

00:12:33.642 --> 00:12:36.209
that they were a big deal
and I don't think of them as

00:12:36.209 --> 00:12:39.197
being a big deal right now.

00:12:39.197 --> 00:12:42.387
You know, there were Saturdays
or Fridays where, you know,

00:12:42.387 --> 00:12:44.867
I'd give up going to a dance
or hang out with my friends

00:12:44.867 --> 00:12:46.449
cause I had workout the next day.

00:12:46.449 --> 00:12:50.048
But those things that I gave
up, you know, were things

00:12:50.048 --> 00:12:54.004
that I wanted to, to
help me get to my goal.

00:12:54.004 --> 00:12:56.835
And there were times where
I've been put in uncomfortable

00:12:56.835 --> 00:13:01.495
situations but I've used my
mental power and my mental

00:13:01.495 --> 00:13:03.263
strength to push through it.

00:13:03.263 --> 00:13:05.814
I think that's how you can
look at any of the athletes

00:13:05.814 --> 00:13:06.850
in the world.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:10.710
I mean Tiger, that guy has
a busted knee and still

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:13.791
comes in and destroys
the rest of the field.

00:13:13.791 --> 00:13:15.408
You know that's the thing.

00:13:15.408 --> 00:13:18.436
It's like people don't make excuses.

00:13:18.436 --> 00:13:21.229
Some of the best athletes
or the greatest athletes

00:13:21.229 --> 00:13:24.088
in the world do things
when they're uncomfortable.

00:13:24.088 --> 00:13:27.357
You know everybody can compete
when they're feeling good,

00:13:27.357 --> 00:13:29.274
happy, excited, rested.

00:13:30.786 --> 00:13:33.377
But it's the best people who
can overcome when they're

00:13:33.377 --> 00:13:36.993
tired, sore, not in the great mind.

00:13:36.993 --> 00:13:38.716
You know, not in the best mindset.

00:13:38.716 --> 00:13:42.937
And I think mental power that
the greatest athletes have

00:13:42.937 --> 00:13:45.616
can push all the pain aside.

00:13:45.616 --> 00:13:49.618
You know like when I was
doing that Navy Seals thing

00:13:49.618 --> 00:13:51.965
was it easy for me to do it, no.

00:13:51.965 --> 00:13:54.182
Was it easy for me to
climb over a 45 foot wall

00:13:54.182 --> 00:13:55.194
and look down?

00:13:55.194 --> 00:13:57.139
Not at all and I'm afraid of heights.

00:13:57.139 --> 00:13:59.907
But, you know, I said to
myself I'm going to do this

00:13:59.907 --> 00:14:01.514
and no one's going to stop me.

00:14:01.514 --> 00:14:04.484
And I think that's the
biggest thing is how strong

00:14:04.484 --> 00:14:05.839
you can be mentally.

00:14:05.839 --> 00:14:08.407
I think that really
shows who the person is.

00:14:08.407 --> 00:14:11.109
So I think that's the one
thing that separates the good

00:14:11.109 --> 00:14:12.493
from the greatest.

